# Documentation

Before creating or revising any committed markdown under `docs/`, load the
`documentation-writing` skill at `.cursor/skills/documentation-writing/SKILL.md`.

It carries the whole discipline: the hard gate on whether a document is allowed, the four committed
types and their paths, the register and voice, and the per-type checklists.

**This file is a pointer and nothing else.** It holds no rules of its own, so the skill stays the
single source of truth and cannot drift from it. Deleting this file costs nothing but the automatic
reminder — the skill is self-contained and works without it.
